      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_99d97d970e53347b10ab0f6c308f64745781c42ccdedee37425c3b90a28e0fcd",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Low-zero family statistics require separate accounting for persistent central mass, functional-equation parity, and symmetry-sensitive correlations. Geometric rank contributes persistent central zeros that are removed before fluctuation analysis; root number partitions a self-dual family by parity; and, in the cited cusp-form calculation, a parity-coupled Kloosterman off-diagonal supplies the term distinguishing SO(even) from SO(odd).",
