    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b299ccb31d2f05057be447b83cd23ccf45fd524e0741ea64126e2b0adc6938b1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The general L-function template separates Euler-factor multiplicativity from completed reflection symmetry. For a normalized modular Hecke eigenform, simultaneous Hecke diagonalization makes Fourier coefficients multiplicative and yields local Euler factors, while modular transformation together with Mellin-type completion yields the functional equation; the two outputs come from compatible structures on the same form.",
