    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b3709447130a708df7a27cf52702ed2412ccba8c2256a3b260166a3e211fa7d2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A polynomial integral transform carries x↦1−x invariance to s↦1−s, so recentering converts its finite critical-line question into real-rootedness, paralleling the representational role of s=1/2+it for completed zeta. Separately, the cited normalized recurrence proves real interlacing by anchoring at large parameter, following zeros continuously, and excluding the only possible common-root collision through a cubic characteristic equation.",
