    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c7abe85a60cfd4bda8defed26c11a7fdd41f8cb0a871b005ac118303954934c0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The explicit formula is an exact prime-zero distributional bridge: logarithmic differentiation, residues, and test functions turn prime-power data and zero data into dual observables. Such encoding constrains location only when supplemented by a sign, self-adjointness, positivity, or geometric index mechanism; spectral statistics and finite-field cohomology specify plausible obligations but do not construct the missing classical object.",
