    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ecdd83b17ad80dc286b7c83a5f21df60a096323fcdd63fe81c4f016ab1778d25",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Petersson-type weighting is both an analytic access mechanism and a choice of family measure. In the cusp-form calculation it produces a diagonal plus Kloosterman-Bessel off-diagonal for Hecke coefficients; in the cited spin family the naturally weighted low-zero density can appear inconsistent with the representation-theoretic prediction when the weight is related conjecturally to a fluctuating central L-value.",
